.TH USILIC 1
.SH NAME
usilic - Text Console Buffer
.SH VERSION
version 1.5b-1  20 Mar 2000
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIusilic\fR
.br
\fIusilic\fR [\fIdirectory\fR]
.br
\fIusilic\fR [\fIfile\fR] [<\fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fIUsilic\fR(1) is a file viewer that works on a text-terminal such as \fIxterm\fR(1).
.SH FILE
.TP 3
\fI/usr/lib/usilic/HELP\fR
On-line manual file.
.TP 3
\fI/usr/lib/usilic/usilicrc\fR
Initialization file, used for setting of environment at \fIusilic\fR(1) startup.  Copy \fIusilicrc\fR to \fI~/.usilic/\fR directory and then edit it accordingly. (The directory \fI~/.usilic/\fR will be made at the first execution.)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP 3
USILICCHARSET
A set of character code can be determined after \fIusilic\fR(1) startup.  However, if USILICCHARSET is set, its value is used for it.  \fBascii\fP or \fBeuc-jp\fP can be set.
.SH AUTHOR
Taketo Matsubara <moody@osk.3web.ne.jp>
